Now, the candy costs 6 tickets each. To find out how many candies he can buy, I need to divide the total tickets by the cost per candy. So 42 divided by 6. Let me do that calculation. 6 times 7 is 42, so 42 divided by 6 is 7. That means he can buy 7 pieces of candy.

