The problem involves calculating Rachel's total score from a video game where she earns 9 points per treasure found. To solve this, we need to determine the points from each level and then add them together. 

First, on the first level, Rachel finds 5 treasures:
$$
5 \text{ treasures} \times 9 \text{ points per treasure} = 45 \text{ points}
$$

Next, on the second level, she finds 2 treasures:
$$
2 \text{ treasures} \times 9 \text{ points per treasure} = 18 \text{ points}
$$

Adding the points from both levels:
$$
45 \text{ points} + 18 \text{ points} = 63 \text{ points}
$$

Alternatively, we can find the total number of treasures found and multiply by 9:
$$
(5 + 2) \text{ treasures} \times 9 \text{ points per treasure} = 7 \times 9 = 63 \text{ points}
$$

Both methods confirm that Rachel's total score is:
$$
\boxed{63}
$$
