Frank started with $19 from mowing lawns. After spending $11 on new mower blades, the amount of money he has left is calculated as follows:

$$
19 - 11 = 8
$$

Frank wants to buy games that cost $2 each. To determine how many games he can buy, we divide the remaining money by the cost per game:

$$
8 \div 2 = 4
$$

Thus, the number of $2 games Frank can buy with the money he has left is:

$$
\boxed{4}
$$

