Total players = 48 + 6

Let me calculate that. 48 plus 6 is 54. So there are 54 players in total.

Now, the coach is putting them into groups with 6 players each. To find out how many groups there are, I need to divide the total number of players by the number of players per group. That makes sense because each group has 6 players, so dividing the total by 6 should give the number of groups.

So, the number of groups is Total players divided by 6.

Number of groups = Total players / 6
Number of groups = 54 / 6

