Nancy initially has 80 files on her computer. She deletes 31 of them, leaving her with:

$$
80 - 31 = 49 \text{ files}
$$

She then puts these 49 files into folders, with 7 files in each folder. To find out how many folders she ends up with, we divide the number of remaining files by the number of files per folder:

$$
49 \div 7 = 7
$$

Thus, Nancy ends up with $\boxed{7}$ folders. 

